- 2026-11-07 22:44 UTC: on the lab since the roll of 39e04adb (the rig with runners at 22:00 UTC), the teachers' round that restarted at 21:59 UTC: the teacher in Claude Code called `WebSearch` at 22:11:22 UTC ("DGX Spark GB10 cudaMalloc first touch page fault slow large allocation unified memory") among its 112 tool calls since 21:30 UTC; the teacher in Codex made no web search in its 8-minute round. Codex's search is not yet seen to be offered: the next rounds show it, or the request's tools at the model proxy.
- 2026-11-07 23:18 UTC: that round's portfolio, at 22:22 UTC, cites a page of NVIDIA's developer forums on slow mmap on the DGX Spark in one of its experiments: the Claude Code teacher's search reached the queue. The Codex teacher's search is still to be seen.
- 2026-11-08 08:29 UTC: in the 10 rounds from 21:58 UTC to 08:03 UTC, the Claude Code teacher made 2 web searches and 6 fetches, in 5 rounds of the 10 (NVIDIA's forums and CUDA guide, vLLM's code and an issue, an LTX-2 issue, the recipe's script); the Codex teacher made none in 11, and each of its rounds began with an `exec` call that Codex refused, `code-mode host is disabled`, six of them looking for a web tool. Why: Codex 0.162.1's model catalog marks gpt-6.1-sol `use_responses_lite` and `code_mode_only`. Codex then sends no hosted tools, `web_search = "live"` included, and offers its standalone search (`web.run`, which calls the provider's `alpha/search`) only for OpenAI's own provider or one marked `supports_standalone_web_search`; Thermite's provider was neither, so the teacher had no search at all, and in Code Mode Only it would reach `web.run` only from `exec`. Live would not have shown a Codex search either: the rollout reader read neither a namespaced tool's name nor `web_search_call`. OpenAI's page on ChatGPT plan usage lists only `POST /responses` and `GET /models`, and says web search depends on the model and the account; whether `alpha/search` answers a ChatGPT sign-in is seen on the lab. Built items 5 to 7. Tests: `tests/agents/model/chatgpt.test.ts`, `tests/agents/programs/codex/rollout.test.ts`, `tests/agents/cli/call.test.ts`, `tests/agents/roles/teacher.test.ts`, `tests/agents/roles/texts.test.ts`, `tests/supervisor/advisors/terminal/profiles.test.ts`; they run on the lab's VM.
- 2026-11-08 10:31 UTC: items 5 to 7 on the lab with 34d17902 (on top of 7b179a33): control at 10:10 UTC, the rig with runners at 10:25 UTC; the other rig drains onto it. The VM's tests of their files passed, 125 of 125, at 7b179a33 and again at 34d17902. The real Codex 0.162.1 of the supervisor image loads a teacher's configuration with no error (`codex doctor`: config.toml parse ok), though it reads unknown keys without a word too: only a round shows `web.run` reach the model. The next rounds: about 11:03 UTC on the rig with runners.
- 2026-11-08 11:18 UTC: the 11:03 UTC round on the rig with runners, the first with items 5 to 7. The teacher in Claude Code made 4 web searches and a fetch (the GB10's drive, a Zig thread question, `pthread_create`'s errors). The teacher in Codex had `web.run` on its list and called it 3 times (two searches at 11:08, a page at 11:12), but said "Live web searches and a direct fetch aborted" and used the run's archived pages instead. Its rollout, read while the call ran, holds each `web.run` call and no output for any of them: Codex 0.162.1 keeps no result of its own search in its log. So the every-round check, which counted only tool calls with a result, sent it back to search at 11:15:32, where it called `web.run` 3 times more. Fixed: the call's proxy hears each search's answer, Live shows it as `web.run`'s result (its status, and an error's words), and a search the proxy carried counts for the round. The next round shows what the provider answers a ChatGPT sign-in's search; if it refuses it, the teacher needs the hosted search instead (Codex drives this model over Responses Lite, which takes no hosted tools).
- 2026-11-08 13:34 UTC: why the Codex teacher's searches fail: in the 13:03 UTC round on the rig with runners, its 9 `web.run` calls, from 13:09 to 13:20 UTC, each got `401 Unauthorized` from OpenAI on `POST /alpha/search`, a text answer of 239 bytes passed on by the call's proxy, while its 54 `POST /responses` got `200`. Built item 8 (`supervisor/advisors/codex-catalog.ts`, `supervisor/advisors/cli.ts`, `supervisor/advisors/terminal/profiles.ts`, `supervisor/advisors/runtimes/opencode-codex.ts`, `agents/programs/codex/index.ts`). Test: `tests/supervisor/advisors/codex-catalog.test.ts`; it runs on the lab's VM.
- 2026-11-08 14:08 UTC: the real Codex 0.162.1 of the supervisor image, offline, against a stand-in that records each request: with the teacher's catalog its request to `POST /responses` carries the hosted `web_search`. Its tool list also held `apply_patch`, the sub-agents' `collaboration` tools, `clock` and `request_user_input_async`, from the entry's own fields, which Code Mode Only had hidden inside `exec`; with those fields gone, `web_search` is its only tool, and no shell tool was on the list in any run. Without the catalog its request has no tools at all. The files of 89d35ab9 passed on the lab's VM, 54 of 54.
- 2026-11-08 16:02 UTC: with 5fcd4538 on the lab (in the roll of 2acab9a3, the P100 run's rig at 15:57 UTC), the Codex teacher's first call failed in 10 s with no answer: OpenAI refused the request (`invalid_request_error` on `tools`, `subscription_sharing_unsupported_capability`): a ChatGPT sign-in's route takes only developer-defined function and custom tools, and "tool 'tool_search' is not supported". Without Code Mode, Codex adds `tool_search` for a teacher's MCP tools; the probe of 14:08 UTC had no MCP server, so it did not show it. Item 8 now gives no catalog on a ChatGPT sign-in's route, and that teacher's call is as it was at 13:03 UTC. So a Codex teacher on a ChatGPT plan has no working web search: its standalone search is answered 401 and the hosted one is refused. The last box of Done when, for a Codex teacher on a ChatGPT plan, waits for the owner: a route with an API key for that teacher, or a web search of Thermite's own for the teachers (a new goal).
- 2026-11-08 17:18 UTC: 493c5435 on the P100 run's rig at 16:56 UTC. In the round of 16:58 UTC the Codex teacher answered after 4 min, with its recommendations and journal. Its `web.run` calls were answered `401` and Live showed the provider's words for each: `This ChatPass credential is not authorized for the requested operation.` (`rejected_by_hardened_oauth_boundary`, `hardened_oauth_rule_missing`). The teacher said its searches and fetches aborted and used the knowledge base and the run's code; with searches carried, it was not sent back. The teacher in Claude Code answered in the same round. The tests of 493c5435 passed on the lab's VM, 17 of 17, and the stand-in's request with a ChatGPT sign-in and MCP servers carried no hosted tool.
- 2026-11-08 18:30 UTC: correction to the entry of 16:02 UTC. Its reading of OpenAI's refusal was wrong: the message Live showed then was cut at its start. The whole message, at 18:08 UTC on the rig with runners, is "User subscription sharing currently supports only 'web_search' and developer-defined 'function' and 'custom' tools, including 'namespace' and 'programmatic_tool_calling'; tool 'tool_search' is not supported." A ChatGPT sign-in's route takes the hosted search; only `tool_search` was refused. So item 8 gives the catalog on every route again, now with `supports_search_tool` false, and a Codex teacher on a ChatGPT plan can search. The stand-in's check never showed `tool_search`: it ran `codex exec`. Run in a terminal, as a teacher runs it, Codex 0.162.1 adds `tool_search` for its deferred worktree tools (`codex_worktrees`); with `supports_search_tool` false it lists those tools instead, `create_worktree` among them; with the feature `worktrees` off too, the request has the hosted `web_search` and the MCP tools alone. Item 8 turns `worktrees` off for every Codex advisor.
- 2026-11-08 20:32 UTC: 6d1f42ea on the lab: control at 20:09 UTC, the P100 run's rig at 20:15 UTC, the rig with runners at 20:25 UTC. The tests of 6d1f42ea passed on the lab's VM, 17 of 17; run in a terminal against the stand-in with a ChatGPT sign-in and two MCP servers, Codex's request carried the hosted `web_search` and the MCP tools alone. In the first round on each rig, the Codex teacher on a ChatGPT plan ran the provider's own search: on the P100 run's rig three searches from 20:17 UTC (P100 half2 GEMM, partial Strassen on GPUs, a paper on compiling Strassen-like algorithms to CUDA), each `web_search: completed`, and on the rig with runners from 20:31 UTC, with no refusal. The teachers in Claude Code worked in the same rounds. Left: the last box of Done when, over the next rounds on both rigs.
- 2026-11-09 07:14 UTC: one round lost to a token, and the fix. On the rig with runners, the Codex teacher of the 04:52 UTC round searched twice, then its call failed at 05:01:48 UTC with `401 Unauthorized: Provided authentication token is expired`, and the round merged the Claude Code teacher's portfolio alone. The P100 run's Codex teacher, on the same sign-in, started at 04:55:56 UTC and answered at 05:03 UTC: control had renewed the token between the two starts, under 9 minutes before the old one ended, because it renews no earlier than OpenAI's `earliest_refresh_at`. Cause: an advisor's call took its key once, at the round's start, and its proxy added that key to every request of the call. Fix: a ChatGPT sign-in's runtime from control reads the newest token of that sign-in in the rig's advisor routes (`keyNow`), and the call's proxy, and Pi's calls straight to OpenAI, take it at each request, as the workers' proxy does since goal 234. In the next two rounds on each rig, from 05:52 and 06:53 UTC, all four teachers searched: 3 to 16 searches or fetches each. (ChatGPT's usage endpoint answers this sign-in 401 at every read, as since 2026-10-14: no sign of an expired token.)
- 2026-11-09 07:50 UTC: fb540a30 on the lab. Its tests passed on the lab's VM, 145 of 145 (the advisors' 27 test files, `tests/supervisor/advisors.test.ts` and `tests/agents/model/chatgpt.test.ts`). Control restarted on it and passed its checks at 07:45:42 UTC, with the rig with runners' judge off from 07:20:36 UTC so that its two jobs under way ended first; the rig with runners moved at 07:47 UTC, reported on fb540a30 at 07:49:04 UTC, and its judge went on again at 07:49:22 UTC; the P100 run's rig drains onto it. To verify: the Codex teachers' rounds on both rigs from 07:52 UTC, a call that outlasts a renewal with no 401.
- 2026-11-09: since the roll onto fb540a30 (07:47 UTC), every teacher round on both campaigns searched or fetched the web: 1 to 16 times in each of the 36 rounds that ended by 17:03 UTC, the four teachers in Claude Code and in Codex, and none failed for its token. Issue 56 closed at the owner's word ("Close issues that are fixed in v0.2.0"). Left: a round that runs across a token renewal, which control does not log yet.

